        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1ce3b5f1-b282-3892-9ba7-5e56ead9a663> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of brocaded silk and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1860"@en , "Dress fabric of brocaded silk and metal thread.\n\nBrocaded silk, plain weave ground.\nWarp: red silk, indeterminable twist.\nWeft: silk orange, black, green, pink, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk; evidence on the back of close S-wound strip.\nDeep pink ground with four offset rows of isolated flowering plant motifs, each with three blossoms in two different colourways, alternately white flowers and black roots or black flowers and white roots, both with bright green leaves and all outlined with metal thread.\nThere is evidence that hot metal rods were used to impress lines on the fabric to create a large, narrow lattice; this is more easily seen on the back."@en ;
